      "body": "## Motivation\n\nSGLang already [builds and tests an Arm64 CPU Docker image in PR CI](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.github/workflows/pr-test-arm64.yml), but it does not publish a versioned image that users can pull This PR adds a release workflow to publish Arm64 CPU images.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- Add a workflow that builds `docker/arm64.Dockerfile` for a release tag or manually supplied SGLang version.\n- Check that the built image runs on Arm64 and loads the CPU attention kernel before pushing it to Docker Hub as `lmsysorg/sglang:v<version>-arm64-cpu`.\n- Include the new workflow file in the Arm64 PR CI change filter.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nNo model or kernel code is changed. Locally, I built the image for `v0.5.22`, started `Qwen/Qwen2.5-0.5B-Instruct` on CPU, and received a successful chat-completion response.\n\nArm64 PR CI: pending\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNot applicable; this PR changes release automation, not inference performance.\n\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [ ☑️] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [ ☑️] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:white_check_mark: [Run #41856254094](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41856254094)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #41856253673](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41856253673)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:heavy_minus_sign: **No AMD PR run found for this commit**.<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Base CI only covers the core cases, and its workload may not exercise your change. Use `/rerun-test` to run the tests your change touches, or copy this prompt for an agent:\n>\n> ```text\n> Find the registered tests this PR affects and run them with /rerun-test, following https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.agents/skills/rerun-test/SKILL.md\n> ```\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
